第八条:
Article 8  A manufacturer applying for a network access licence for telecommunications equipment shall submit the following application materials to an acceptance body authorised by the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology:

(1) an application form for a telecommunications equipment network access licence (in the format provided by the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology). The application form shall be signed by the legal representative of the manufacturer or a person authorised by them and bear the official seal. A manufacturer outside China shall entrust an agency within China to submit the application form and shall issue a power of attorney;

(2) the enterprise legal person business licence. A manufacturer within China shall provide its enterprise legal person business licence. An agency applying for a telecommunications equipment network access licence on the entrustment of a manufacturer outside China shall provide the agency’s valid licence;

(3) a description of the enterprise, including its general situation, production conditions, instrument provision, quality assurance system and after-sales service arrangements. For products for which the State requires guaranteed repair, replacement and return, documents evidencing the performance of the relevant responsibilities shall also be provided;

(4) a quality system certification certificate or audit report. Where quality system certification has been obtained, the certificate shall be provided; where it has not, a quality system audit report issued by a quality system audit body meeting the relevant requirements shall be provided;

(5) a description of the telecommunications equipment, including its functions, performance indicators, schematic block diagram, photographs of its interior and exterior, and operating instructions;

(6) a test report or product certification certificate. This shall be a test report issued by a telecommunications equipment testing body recognised by the product quality supervision department of the State Council, or a product certification certificate issued by a certification body.

For radio transmission equipment for which a network access licence is applied for, the “radio transmission equipment type approval certificate” issued by the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology shall be provided.

For radio communications equipment, equipment involved in network interconnection, or a new product, an overall technical plan and a trial report shall be provided.

Among the foregoing application materials, certificates and licences shall be provided as originals together with one photocopy, or as photocopies bearing the certifying seal of the issuing body; all other materials must be in Chinese.

第三十二条:
Article 32  Where, in violation of these Measures, a manufacturer commits any of the following acts, the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology or the communications administration of the province, autonomous region or directly governed municipality shall order rectification within a set period; where the circumstances are serious, a warning shall be issued:

(1) providing untrue application materials when applying for a network access licence;

(2) failing to ensure the consistency of telecommunications equipment before and after it obtains a network access licence;

(3) failing to deliver after-sales service, or failing to perform the corresponding obligations for products for which the State requires guaranteed repair, replacement and return;

(4) failing to participate in the annual inspection as required, or failing the annual inspection;

(5) refusing to accept the supervision and inspection organised by the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology into the consistency of telecommunications equipment before and after it obtains a network access licence, or failing such inspection.

Where item (1) of the preceding paragraph is violated and a network access licence has not yet been obtained, the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology shall decline to accept the application or decline to grant the licence, and the manufacturer may not apply again for a network access licence within one year; where a network access licence has already been obtained, the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology shall revoke it, and the manufacturer may not apply again for a network access licence within three years.

第三十五条:
Article 35  Where, in violation of these Measures, a testing body or product quality certification body commits any of the following acts, the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology shall decline to recognise the test report or certification certificate it issues:

(2) conducting testing or certification otherwise than against the prescribed standards;

(3) issuing a test report or certification certificate otherwise than in accordance with the provisions of the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology.
